 given equality by $(x+1)({x}^{2}+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5x-2 & =(2x+B)(x+1)-({x}^{2}+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0$  into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+5(0)-2 & =(2(0)+B)(0+1)-({0}^{2}+5) \\\\ -2 & =B-5 \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x-2}{(x+1)({x}^{2}+5)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2x+3}{{x}^{2}+5}-\\frac{1}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+5}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+5}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution ${x}^{2}+5=u.$ Then, $2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ and we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{5}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+5x-2}{(x+1)({x}^{2}+5)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+5)+\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}x}{5})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534902 true] [17592186318457 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318458 13194139534902 true] [17592186318457 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318459 13194139534902 true] [17592186318457 1000 #edb/ref 17592186